oraciones.textoOriginal:
Domine, fac me instrumentum pacis tuae:
Ubi odium, ibi amorem seram;
Ubi iniuria, ibi veniam;
Ubi discordia, ibi concordiam;
Ubi dubium, ibi fidem;
Ubi desperatio, ibi spem;
Ubi tenebrae, ibi lucem;
Ubi maestitia, ibi laetitiam. Amen.

oraciones.textoTraducido:
1. Say: “He is God, One and Only;
2. God, the Absolute and Infinite;
3. has not begotten nor been begotten;
4. and there is nothing and no one that is like him or equal to him.

1. See how good and how delightful it is for brothers to dwell together in harmony!
2. It is like the good oil on the head, which runs down on the beard, Aaron's beard, and goes down to the hem of his garments;
3. like the dew of Hermon, which descends on the mountains of Zion; because there the Lord sends blessing and eternal life.

1. My son, do not forget my law, and let your heart keep my commandments;
2. because length of days and years of life and peace will increase to you.
3. Let mercy and truth never depart from you; tie them around your neck, write them on the tablet of your heart;
4. and you will find favor and good opinion in the eyes of God and men.
5. Trust in the Lord with all your heart, and do not lean on your own understanding.
6. In all your ways acknowledge him, and he will make your paths straight.
7. Do not be wise in your own opinion; fear the Lord, and depart from evil;
8. for it will be medicine for your body, and refreshment for your bones.

Lord, make me an instrument of your peace:
Where there is hate, I sow love;
Where there is offense, forgiveness;
Where there is discord, union;
Where there is doubt, faith;
Where there is error, truth;
Where there is despair, hope;
Where there is darkness, light;
Where there is sadness, joy.

Oh Master! Grant me that I do not seek so much to be consoled as to console, to be understood as to understand, to be loved as to love. Because giving is how we receive, forgiving is how we are forgiven, and dying is how we are resurrected to eternal life. Amen.

Let nothing disturb thee, nothing affright thee;
All things are passing, God never changeth;
Patient endurance attaineth to all things;
Who God possesseth in nothing is wanting;
Alone God sufficeth. Amen.

Om. Lead me from non-truth to the Supreme Truth;
Lead me from darkness to Light;
Lead me from death to Immortality.
Om. Peace in the body, peace in the mind, peace in the spirit. Om Shanti, Shanti, Shanti.
